---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy"
  description="Learn how Clipping Guide uses analytics and optional browser storage, and how calculator inputs and saved checklist preferences are handled."
>
  <div class="wrap page-intro">
    <h1>Privacy, in plain language.</h1>
    <p>Last updated October 6, 2026.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="wrap plain-page prose">
    <h2>Reading the site</h2>
    <p>
      You can read guides and use tools without creating an account. We do not ask you to upload
      videos or submit personal information to use the calculator or checklist.
    </p>
    <h2>Website analytics</h2>
    <p>
      We use Vercel Web Analytics to understand aggregate visits, popular pages, and traffic
      sources. Vercel describes this service as using no cookies for visitor tracking. Hosting and
      analytics providers may process technical request information under their own policies. See{' '}
      <a href="https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/privacy-policy">
        Vercel's analytics privacy documentation
      </a>{' '}
      and <a href="https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-policy">Vercel's privacy policy</a>.
    </p>
    <h2>Browser storage</h2>
    <p>
      If you change the color theme, the site stores that preference in your browser. The publishing
      checklist only saves checked items when you turn on “Save progress on this device.” Turn that
      setting off to remove the saved checklist. Calculator inputs stay in the page and are not sent
      to our server or included in custom analytics events.
    </p>
    <h2>Links & embedded content</h2>
    <p>
      Official source links take you to other sites with their own privacy policies. If a guide
      includes a video, the video is loaded only when you choose to open it on the source platform.
    </p>
    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>
      You can{' '}
      <a href="https://github.com/vishprometa/clippingguide/issues/new?title=Clipping%20Guide%20privacy%20question">
        open a privacy question
      </a>{' '}
      without including sensitive personal details.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
